{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:26.676Z","data":{"turn":13,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I have a comprehensive overview of the recon deliverable. Let me now set up my Todo list and begin the systematic authorization analysis.\\n\\nKey findings to analyze based on Section 8:\\n\\n**Horizontal (8.1):**\\n1. `GET /api/contracts/:id` - No party check (IDOR)\\n2. `PUT /api/contracts/:id/status` - No party check (IDOR)\\n3. `GET /api/messages/conversations/:id` - No participant check (IDOR)\\n\\n\\n4. `POST /api/messages/conversations/:id/messages` - No participant check (IDOR)\\n5. `GET /api/contracts/:id/invoice` - No party check (IDOR)\\n6. `GET /api/users/:id/settings` - No auth at all\\n7. `POST /api/contracts/:id/milestones/:milestoneId/submit` - No party check (IDOR)\\n8. `PUT /api/contracts/:id/milestones/:milestoneId/approve` - No party check (IDOR)\\n9. `POST /api/contracts/:id/milestones` - No party check (IDOR)\\n10. `PUT /api/contracts/:id/milestones/:milestoneId` - No party check (IDOR)\\n11. `GET /api/proposals` - Missing authorization checks on freelancer filtering, allowing any authenticated user to query by freelancer ID. Several more milestone endpoints lack proper party validation for submissions, approvals, and revisions. Review creation and retrieval also have insufficient access controls, with private reviews being readable without proper authorization. For vertical privilege escalation, there's JWT forgery via hardcoded secrets and potential role rechecks missing in dispute assignment and resolution endpoints, though admin routes appear properly guarded. Context-based vulnerabilities are still being examined.\\n\\nNow I'm identifying the specific state validation gaps across milestone operations and payment flows, plus token reuse issues in authentication endpoints that could allow attackers to bypass email verification or reset password protections.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:26.676Z"}}
