{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:47:05.101Z","data":{"turn":34,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01JJJY5PGygAkxZFCjZywbRc\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Analyze reviews, users settings, disputes, and JWT auth\",\"prompt\":\"Read and analyze the following files for authorization vulnerabilities. Return the COMPLETE content of each file and your analysis.\\n\\nFiles to read:\\n1. /repos/webvulnbench/src/reviews/reviews.routes.js\\n2. /repos/webvulnbench/src/reviews/reviews.controller.js\\n3. /repos/webvulnbench/src/reviews/reviews.service.js (first 100 lines)\\n4. /repos/webvulnbench/src/users/users.routes.js\\n5. /repos/webvulnbench/src/users/users.controller.js (first 150 lines)\\n6. /repos/webvulnbench/src/disputes/disputes.routes.js\\n7. /repos/webvulnbench/src/disputes/disputes.controller.js\\n8. /repos/webvulnbench/src/middleware/auth.js\\n9. /repos/webvulnbench/src/middleware/rbac.js\\n10. /repos/webvulnbench/src/config/index.js\\n\\nSpecifically check:\\n- GET /api/users/:id/settings - is there any authentication middleware?\\n- GET /api/reviews/:id - does it filter out private reviews?\\n- POST /api/reviews - does it check the requesting user is a party to the contract?\\n- PUT /api/disputes/:id/assign - does the controller recheck moderator role?\\n- PUT /api/disputes/:id/resolve - does it check prior state (assigned)?\\n- JWT_SECRET default value - is it hardcoded?\\n- rbac.js - what are the requireRole, requireAdmin, requireModerator implementations?\\n\\nFor each endpoint report: what middleware is applied, what checks exist in the controller/service before the DB read/write side effect.\",\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:47:05.101Z"}}
