{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:47:09.674Z","data":{"turn":46,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01RSrGCDeVJ6KeHHDcvGZd8K\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Analyze payments and webhook authorization\",\"prompt\":\"Read and analyze the following files for authorization vulnerabilities. Return the COMPLETE content of each file and your analysis.\\n\\nFiles to read:\\n1. /repos/webvulnbench/src/payments/payments.routes.js\\n2. /repos/webvulnbench/src/payments/payments.controller.js\\n3. /repos/webvulnbench/src/payments/payments.service.js (first 200 lines)\\n4. /repos/webvulnbench/src/integrations/webhook.routes.js\\n5. /repos/webvulnbench/src/integrations/webhook.service.js (first 60 lines)\\n6. /repos/webvulnbench/src/auth/auth.controller.js (first 80 lines)\\n7. /repos/webvulnbench/src/auth/auth.service.js (first 80 lines)\\n\\nSpecifically check:\\n- POST /api/payments/escrow/release/:milestoneId - does it check milestone approval state before releasing funds?\\n- POST /api/webhooks/payment - is the signature verification truly optional (skippable)?\\n- POST /api/auth/reset-password - is the token invalidated after use?\\n- What is the JWT_SECRET default value in config?\\n\\nFor each endpoint report: what middleware is applied, what checks exist in the controller/service before the financial side effect.\",\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:47:09.674Z"}}
